          "says": "answered 404, drew \"Node.js Developer\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/careers/uiux-designer/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"UI/UX Designer\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/projects/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"Projects\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/projects/siv/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"Members Only, By Design.\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/careers/devops-engineer/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"DevOps Engineer\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/careers/product-owner/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"Product Owner\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/careers/nextjs-frontend-developer/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"Next.js Frontend Developer\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz/careers/react-native-developer/",
          "says": "answered 404, drew \"React Native Developer\""
        }
      ],
      "why": "A visitor sees each page, but search engines, link checkers and monitoring trust the status: they treat these pages as missing, so they may never appear in search results, and every check calls them broken.",
      "fix": "Serve each page with status 200: a single-page app behind a CDN usually needs its error response (the one that returns index.html) set to 200, or each route pre-rendered as its own file."
    },
    {
      "code": "SITE-06",
      "severity": "major",
      "title": "1 of the 13 addresses spiralmm.xyz points to does not answer: about 1 connection in 13 can fail",
      "where": [
        {
          "url": "https://spiralmm.xyz",
          "says": "192.64.119.6 (IPv4): no answer in 5 s; the others answered"
        }
      ],
      "why": "Each new visit picks one of the addresses. On one that does not answer, the page hangs and fails after a long wait. Chrome often tries the next address, so the site looks fine from a browser; scripts, some phones, monitoring and test tools do not.",
      "fix": "Remove the address that does not answer from the domain's DNS records (often a registrar's parking or redirect record left beside the hosting's), or make it serve the site."
    },
